            <ArticleTitle>Chronic painful sesamoids of the thumb.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In patients with persistent localized pain at the level of a sesamoid bone of the thumb not obviously related to trauma, sesamoidectomy gives excellent results. Often no X-ray or histological abnormalities are found, leaving the origin of pain problems still unsolved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
